* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_flobnd (reference/crafted.toml, 14 Nov 2026): bounds on process
* flows (FLO_BND) that cannot be bounds of one flow variable, which GAMS writes as the equations
* EQ(l)_FLOBND (eqflobnd.mod L15-43; bnd_flo.mod L16-24 marks the records). Added to TIMES_Demo
* demo12 (etsap-TIMES/TIMES_Demo @ 962db86, CC BY 4.0). The power plants run at DAYNITE (SD, SN,
* WD, WN, in the seasons S and W) or SEASON; ELCTNGAS01 is the vintaged process.
* Standard processes:
* - ELCTEGAS00, gas input at ANNUAL, UP in REG1 2020: above the flow's level, a sum over the
*   four DAYNITE timeslices. Under REDUCE the flow is replaced by the activity (cal_red.red).
* - ELCREHYD00, electricity output (the activity flow) at the season W, LO in REG1 2030.
* - ELCTNGAS01, gas input at WD, UP in REG2 2020: the flow's own level, but the process is
*   vintaged, so an equation over the vintages (bnd_flo.mod L18).
* - ELCTNGAS01, electricity output at the season W, FX in REG1 2030.
* - FTE-AGROIL, diesel input at ANNUAL, UP in REG1 2020: the flow's own level on a process
*   without vintages: a bound of VAR_FLO and no equation.
* - ELCTEOIL00, oil input at SD, UP in REG1 2030: the flow's own level. Under REDUCE the flow
*   variable is replaced by the activity (RPC_FFUNC), so the bound is an equation (L19);
*   without REDUCE it is a bound of VAR_FLO.
* - ELCREBIO00, electricity output at WN, UP in REG1 2020: the activity flow at its own level:
*   a bound of VAR_ACT under REDUCE (bnd_flo.mod L37-39), of VAR_FLO without.
* - ELCTEGAS00, the CO2 emission (RPC_EMIS, never a bound of the variable, L20) at ANNUAL, UP in
*   REG1 2020, and at SD (its own level), LO with the value EPS in REG2 2020: the LO EPS record
*   of an emission flow is kept (L16) and gives a row with a right-hand side of zero.
* - ELCTEGAS00, gas input at ANNUAL in REG2 2020: UP with the value INF, an equation with an
*   empty body (eqmain.mod L113), and LO with the value EPS, which L16 deletes.
* - REFEOIL00, the output group REFEOIL00_NRGO at ANNUAL: UP in REG1 2030 and LO with the value
*   EPS in REG1 2020. A group is always an equation (L23), and its LO EPS is kept (L16 covers
*   single commodities only).
* - ELCRESOL00, solar input at ANNUAL, UP in REG1 2030, a period in which the process is not
*   available (RTP_VARA): nothing.
* - ELCTECOA00 (SEASON), coal input at SD, UP in REG1 2020: a timeslice below the flow's level:
*   nothing.
* Exchange processes (never bounds of one variable):
* - IMPELC1, the electricity import at ANNUAL, UP in REG1 2030, and at WN (its own level), UP
*   in REG2 2020. Under REDUCE the import is the activity (RPC_AIRE).
* - TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01 (import and export in both regions), ELC at the season S, UP in REG1
*   2020 with interpolation and forward extrapolation (option 5): import plus export in 2020,
*   2030 and 2050.
* - TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01, the group NRG at the season W in REG2 2030, UP and LO: with a group
*   the bound is on the net import, import less export (L37).
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
PARAMETER
FLO_BND ' '/
REG1.2020.ELCTEGAS00.ELCGAS.ANNUAL.UP 500
REG1.2030.ELCREHYD00.ELC.W.LO 60
REG2.2020.ELCTNGAS01.ELCGAS.WD.UP 1500
REG1.2030.ELCTNGAS01.ELC.W.FX 950
REG1.2020.FTE-AGROIL.DSL.ANNUAL.UP 160
REG1.2030.ELCTEOIL00.ELCOIL.SD.UP 50
REG1.2020.ELCREBIO00.ELC.WN.UP 20
REG1.2020.ELCTEGAS00.ELCCO2.ANNUAL.UP 100000
REG2.2020.ELCTEGAS00.ELCCO2.SD.LO EPS
REG2.2020.ELCTEGAS00.ELCGAS.ANNUAL.UP INF
REG2.2020.ELCTEGAS00.ELCGAS.ANNUAL.LO EPS
REG1.2030.REFEOIL00.REFEOIL00_NRGO.ANNUAL.UP 9500
REG1.2020.REFEOIL00.REFEOIL00_NRGO.ANNUAL.LO EPS
REG1.2030.ELCRESOL00.ELCSOL.ANNUAL.UP 10
REG1.2020.ELCTECOA00.ELCCOA.SD.UP 100
REG1.2030.IMPELC1.ELC.ANNUAL.UP 500
REG2.2020.IMPELC1.ELC.WN.UP 550
REG1.0.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.ELC.S.UP 5
REG1.2020.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.ELC.S.UP 30
REG2.2030.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.NRG.W.UP 25
REG2.2030.TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01.NRG.W.LO -25
/
